# 49. RBAC

Create/use permissions such as:

```text
attendance.location.view
attendance.location.create
attendance.location.update
attendance.location.delete

attendance.location_policy.view
attendance.location_policy.update

attendance.verification.view
attendance.verification.manage

attendance.exception.view
attendance.exception.manage
```

Use Phase 2's existing RBAC system.

Do not hard-code role names throughout the code.

---

# 50. TENANT ISOLATION

Every location-related object must respect tenant boundaries.

For example:

```text
Tenant A
   |
   +-- Branch A
       |
       +-- Location A
```

Tenant A must never be able to:

```text
read Location B
update Location B
assign Location B
use Location B for attendance
```

even if the IDs are known.

Test this explicitly.

---

# 51. CROSS-TENANT VALIDATION

When assigning:

```text
Employee
+
Branch
+
Location
+
Policy
```

verify all objects belong to the same tenant.

Never rely solely on frontend filtering.

---

# 52. TRANSACTIONS

Operations such as:

```text
Create location
Assign location
Check-in
Create attendance event
Create verification record
```

must use appropriate transaction boundaries.

Avoid partially completed attendance operations.

---

# 53. IDEMPOTENCY

Protect:

```text
GPS check-in
GPS check-out
Selfie upload
Verification request
```

against duplicate network requests.

Mobile networks frequently retry requests.

The same logical attendance request must not create multiple attendance events.

---

# 54. TIME SECURITY

Use server time as authoritative for attendance.

The client-provided:

```text
captured_at
```

should be treated as metadata and validated for freshness.

Do not allow users to manipulate attendance by changing their device clock.

---

# 55. LOCATION MOCKING TESTABILITY

Do not make the test suite depend on real GPS hardware.

Create test fixtures/mocks for:

```text
inside geofence
outside geofence
low accuracy
stale location
invalid coordinates
GPS unavailable
```

---

# 56. TEST DATA

Create test locations such as:

```text
Office A
Latitude: test value
Longitude: test value
Radius: 100m
```

Use deterministic test coordinates.

Do not use real employee location data.

---

# 57. UNIT TESTS

Test:

```text
coordinate validation
distance calculation
geofence calculation
accuracy validation
freshness validation
policy evaluation
verification decision
```

Examples:

```text
0 meters
10 meters
99 meters
100 meters
101 meters
```

Verify boundary behavior.

---

# 58. GEOFENCE EDGE TESTS

Test:

